Bluetooth: require supported command for extended advertising

Some controllers (e.g. the nRF52840 on Edgecore EAP102, running nRF Connect
SDK hci_usb with the SoftDevice Controller) set the LE Extended Advertising
bit in LE Read Local Supported Features, but do not implement any of the
extended advertising HCI commands in Read Local Supported Commands.

Kernel 5.4 decides extended advertising support from the feature bit alone,
so during init it sends LE Read Number of Supported Advertising Sets
(0x203B). The controller replies Unknown HCI Command (0x01) and controller
initialization aborts (errno 56, EBADRQC).

Also require the LE Read Number of Supported Advertising Sets command bit
(octet 36, bit 7) before treating the controller as extended advertising
capable. Controllers that implement the commands are unaffected; others
fall back to legacy advertising.

--- a/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
+++ b/include/net/bluetooth/hci_core.h
@@ -1216,5 +1216,5 @@
 
 /* Extended advertising support */
-#define ext_adv_capable(dev) (((dev)->le_features[1] & HCI_LE_EXT_ADV))
+#define ext_adv_capable(dev) (((dev)->le_features[1] & HCI_LE_EXT_ADV) && ((dev)->commands[36] & 0x80))
 
 /* ----- HCI protocols ----- */
